Then I disagree with you on what a bones file is supposed to
represent.  A bones file is from a previous game and as such
it was in existance before the player character entered the level.
Depending on how often adventurers are sent into the dungeon,
maybe even before the game started.  As such it does not have
to be an "exact" match in the sense of containing unique items.

So to me it makes sense that any artifact given by a deity
could include one that had been in the possession of a previous
adventurer that got repossessed by the deity at the time it is
given as a gift at an altar/fountain/quest.

Dealing with previous characters who ascended with artifacts, the
game does assume the Amulet has never been given to a diety
so no need to remember those.

Dealing with previous adventurers who escape the dungeon with
artifacts, some pawn shop could be very surprised indeed when
the issuing deity decides to gift it to the next hero and poof it
goes from the pawn shop on the surface to an altar in the dungeon.


